>
  <h2 id="status">FY2027 Section 8 funding status on 2026-10-28</h2>
  <p>
    Section 8 funding for FY2027 runs on a stopgap law. The Continuing Appropriations and Extensions Act, 2027 (H.R. 6500,
    P.L. 119-103) became law on 2026-09-02. It funds HUD through 2026-12-11. CRS says it funds HUD programs "at the same
    rate and under the same conditions as in FY2026, with some exceptions".
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>House.</strong> The House Appropriations Committee approved its FY2027 HUD bill, H.R. 9170, on 2026-06-03 (CRS).</li>
    <li><strong>Senate.</strong> At the time of the CRS report (2026-09-03), the Senate Appropriations Committee had no FY2027 HUD bill.</li>
    <li><strong>Next step.</strong> Congress must act by 2026-12-11: a full-year bill or another stopgap. NAHRO (2026-10-19) calls the final FY2027 decisions "TBD".</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="numbers">FY2027 voucher funding: request, House bill, 2026 level</h2>
  <p>
    FY2027 voucher money is close to the 2026 level in all three plans. The big gap is the fee that pays housing authority
    staff. Numbers from CRS R49341, Table 3.
  </p>
  <table>
