  <h2 id="landlord-steps">Steps for landlords</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Ask about shortfall status.</strong> Ask your housing specialist if the housing authority is working with HUD's Shortfall Prevention Team.</li>
    <li><strong>Watch the payment standard.</strong> A cut raises the tenant share at the next applicable date. Check the <a href="/guides/section-8-rent-limits">FY2027 Fair Market Rents</a> for your metro.</li>
    <li><strong>Plan for fewer new voucher holders.</strong> A housing authority that stops issuing vouchers sends fewer new applicants. Price vacancies with that in mind.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep the unit in compliance.</strong> A HAP contract can also end for owner breach (24 CFR 982.453). Do not give a short budget a second reason.</li>
    <li><strong>Run the numbers.</strong> Estimate the split with the <a href="/tools/section-8-rent-calculator">Section 8 rent calculator</a>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Rules differ by housing authority. This page is not legal advice. Check your housing authority.</p>

